---
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import assets from "../data/assets.json";
import { credits, rooms, site } from "../data/rooms";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
type Art = { width: number; height: number; avif: Record<string, string>; webp: Record<string, string> };
const art = (assets as unknown as { art: Record<string, Art> }).art;
const srcset = (set: Record<string, string>) =>
	Object.entries(set)
		.map(([w, url]) => `${base}${url} ${w}w`)
		.join(", ");

const artAlt: Record<string, string> = {
	wave: "Woodblock print: a towering blue wave curls over three long boats, its crest breaking into claw-like foam; Mount Fuji, small and snow-capped, sits in the distance.",
	rain: "Woodblock print: people under hats and straw mats hurry across a long wooden bridge in heavy rain drawn as fine dark lines, while a raft drifts on the river below a dark band of cloud.",
	stillness: "Oil painting: a green arched footbridge crosses a pond crowded with water lilies, framed by weeping willows and dense foliage in greens, pinks and violets.",
	moonlight: "Oil painting: a full moon glows through a tunnel of clouds above a calm river; tall ships stand in silhouette and torches burn on barges to the right.",
};
const contact = "javierpiedraiglesias@gmail.com";
---

<Page
	title="About and credits"
	description="About Inside the Frame: the four public-domain paintings and the museums that hold them, how the exhibition can be used, and credits."
	current="about"
>
	<header class="doc-hero">
		<h1>Four paintings you can stand inside</h1>
		<p class="doc-lede">
			Online collections show a painting as a flat image with a caption beside it. {site.name} asks what it would be like to
			step into one. You start in a dark gallery whose floor lies under still water. Choose a painting, and you go through
			the canvas into the place it shows.
		</p>
	</header>

	<section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="works">
		<div class="chapter-head">
			<span class="chapter-numeral" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
			<h2 id="works">The works</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="chapter-body">
			<p>
				Four pictures of water, made within seventy years of each other in Japan, France and England: a wave about to fall, rain
				in mid-air, a pond holding its breath, a river under the moon. All four are in the public domain, and the museums that
				hold them have released their images for anyone to use.
			</p>
			<ol class="works" role="list">
				{
					rooms.map((room) => {
						const a = art[room.slug];
						return (
							<li class="work" style={`--pigment: ${room.pigment}`}>
								{a && (
									<picture>
										<source type="image/avif" srcset={srcset(a.avif)} sizes="(min-width: 44em) 17rem, 92vw" />
										<img
											src={`${base}${a.webp["960"]}`}
											srcset={srcset(a.webp)}
											sizes="(min-width: 44em) 17rem, 92vw"
											alt={artAlt[room.slug]}
											width={a.width}
											height={a.height}
											loading="lazy"
											decoding="async"
										/>
									</picture>
								)}
								<div class="work-text">
									<p class="work-no">
										<span class="swatch" aria-hidden="true" />
										Room {room.numeral} — {room.theme}
									</p>
									<h3>
										<cite>{room.title}</cite>
									</h3>
									<p class="work-by">
										{room.artist} ({room.artistDates}), {room.date}
									</p>
									<p>{room.summary}</p>
									<dl class="facts">
										<div>
											<dt>Medium</dt>
											<dd>{room.medium}</dd>
										</div>
										<div>
											<dt>Size</dt>
											<dd>{room.dimensions}</dd>
										</div>
										<div>
											<dt>Collection</dt>
											<dd>
												{room.museum}. {room.credit}. {room.accession}.
											</dd>
										</div>
										<div>
											<dt>Image</dt>
											<dd>Public domain, released by the museum under CC0.</dd>
										</div>
									</dl>
									<p class="work-links">
										<a href={`${base}${room.slug}/`}>
											Enter Room {room.numeral}
											<Icon name="arrow-right" />
										</a>
										<a href={room.museumUrl} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
											See it in the museum's collection
											<span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span>
											<Icon name="external" />
										</a>
									</p>
								</div>
							</li>
						);
					})
				}
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="chapter" id="accessibility" aria-labelledby="a11y">
		<div class="chapter-head">
			<span class="chapter-numeral" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
			<h2 id="a11y">Using the exhibition</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="chapter-body">
			<p>
				The exhibition was built to be used in more than one way. It aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
				2.2 at level AA, and is checked against them with automated tests (axe-core) and by hand with a keyboard.
			</p>
			<ul class="plain-list">
				<li>
					<strong>Without seeing it.</strong> Every room has a written description of its world and of the painting. Screen
					readers get landmarks, headings, a labelled 360° view and an announcement on entering each room.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>With a keyboard.</strong> The arrow keys look around, + and − zoom, Tab reaches the paintings and the points
					of interest, and the view turns to show whatever has focus. Escape closes what is open.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Without dragging.</strong> A button in the corner of the view (on a phone, in the menu) opens look and zoom
					buttons that move one step per click or tap. “Look closer” on each room's label lists its points of interest, numbered as they are in the view.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>With less motion.</strong> Animation can be paused at any time from the top of the screen, and starts paused
					where the system asks for reduced motion. Paused, nothing moves on its own, the controls stay put and rooms change
					with a plain cross-fade.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>In silence.</strong> Sound is offered, never assumed, and nothing depends on it.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>On a small screen, or a large zoom.</strong> It works from 320 pixels wide, in portrait and landscape, with
					touch targets of at least 44 pixels.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Without WebGL or JavaScript.</strong> Each room is then a page of pictures and text.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				If something here gets in your way, I would like to know: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="credits">
		<div class="chapter-head">
			<span class="chapter-numeral" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
			<h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="chapter-body">
			<dl class="facts">
				<div>
					<dt>Concept, 3D, sound and code</dt>
					<dd>
						<a href={site.authorUrl} rel="noopener">{site.author}</a>
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Paintings</dt>
					<dd>
						{rooms.map((r, i) => (
							<>
								{i > 0 && <br />}
								{r.artist}, <cite>{r.title}</cite> — {r.museum}
							</>
						))}
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Textures</dt>
					<dd>
						Poly Haven (CC0):{" "}
						{credits.textures.map((t, i) => (
							<>
								{i > 0 && ", "}
								<a href={t.url} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
									{t.name}
								</a>{" "}
								by {t.author}
							</>
						))}
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Type</dt>
					<dd>
						Ibarra Real Nova, after the types Joaquín Ibarra printed with in Madrid around 1780, and Libre Franklin (both SIL
						Open Font License)
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div>
					<dt>Made with</dt>
					<dd>Blender 5 and Cycles, scripted in Python; Astro; WebGL 2; the Web Audio API</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
			<p>
				<a href={`${base}making-of/`}>How it was made</a> follows one world from the painting to the browser.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="author">
		<div class="chapter-head">
			<span class="chapter-numeral" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
			<h2 id="author">Who made it</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="chapter-body">
			<p>
				{site.name} is a personal project by <a href={site.authorUrl} rel="noopener">{site.author}</a>, a front-end
				developer who works on 3D for the web and on interfaces that everyone can use: the idea, the worlds, the sound and
				the code are by one person. This is the first volume.
			</p>
			<h3>Make one with me</h3>
			<p>
				A painting, a building, an archive, a wine, a new product: whatever has something to be stood inside of can become a
				place like these, in any browser and without an app. I work with museums, foundations, studios and brands, from
				the first drawing to the launch, or on the part of it that you are missing.
			</p>
			<p>
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href={`mailto:${contact}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Inside the Frame")}`}>Write to me</a>
				<a class="btn" href={site.authorUrl} rel="noopener">See my other work</a>
			</p>
			<p>
				Or copy the address: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="doc-next">
		<p>The paintings are waiting.</p>
		<div class="doc-next-actions">
			<a class="btn btn-primary" href={base}>Enter the exhibition</a>
			<a class="btn" href={`${base}making-of/`}>How it was made</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</Page>
